  "method": [
    "Exact original R14 canvas source, each wearer original parameters, all 39 construction parts and original materials retained.",
    "Foot/toe base field is a positive C2 B-spline upper envelope of original body requirements; source material coordinates and triangles remain separate.",
    "Ankle opening uses measured exits through all original body triangles. Its frozen horizontal radial field shares one transform across all source components and attachments.",
    "Control support core is the innermost actual risk sample radius; no arbitrary small activation weight amplifies displacement.",
    "Independent audit queries all actual original inner vertices, all triangle centres and unique edge midpoints against the complete body.",
    "Finite Float32 triangle cross is compared with the Jacobian-transported source cross. This discretization check is separate from the positive continuous map determinant; no raw-normal >90-degree test is used as a folding claim."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Neutral vertex/edge/centre samples do not certify continuous whole-triangle separation or pressure/comfort.",
    "New full-CSR motion pose replay is still required; historical 2136/294 evidence remains historical and was not relabelled.",
    "Current local images show complete original geometry with D24/4xMSAA and flat diagnostic pigment; actual native material/browser performance and appearance remain unreviewed.",
    "B opening is visibly broad and A/B/F rear quarters high. Numerical clearance does not certify aesthetic acceptance."
  ],
  "transformContract": "One original left reflection in shoe scale; restNative then native foot skin, C to display, then actor root. Numerical complete sole points use the same restNative/reflection/foot-skin chain. No repeated fitting field is applied at runtime.",
